emma_cs: Customer (Acme Corp) hit a hard failure: client sees JSONDecodeError when parsing our /v1/generate output. Happens ~1-2% of calls, mostly longer outputs. Ticket 7891. Posting sample and logs from the customer.

jon_customer: repro steps from our app: 1) POST /v1/generate with system+user prompt 2) streaming enabled 3) we assemble chunks and parse final payload. Intermittent last-line truncation or stray commas. Example response attached.

maya_support: thx jon, can you paste the exact request body + model + streaming flag? also what SDK/version?

jon_customer: using our internal client (wraps fetch), model: openglm-32k (via redwood catalog), sdk: custom 0.3.1, streaming: true. Request payload:
```json
{
  "model": "openglm-32k",
  "prompt": "<redacted long prompt>",
  "max_tokens": 1500,
  "stream": true,
  "json_schema": {"type":"object","properties":{"summary":{"type":"string"},"tags":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["summary"]}
}
```

jon_customer: broken fragment we got (final join failed parse):
```json
{"summary":"All systems nominal", "tags":["ops","infra",],
```
(note the trailing comma and missing closing brace)

maya_support: ok that's helpful. two probable classes: 1) model truncation during streaming (trailer lost), 2) post-assembly ordering issue in their client. we'll try to repro ourselves.

kevin_sre: noticing a small spike at 1976499900 on the serving cluster where a gRPC stream had a premature EOF for a handful of requests — looks correlated with the GPU preemption window we had. Suspect some streams truncated.

alex_ml: suggestions for mitigation: 1) defensive postprocessing: run a lightweight regex to strip trailing commas and append closing brackets/braces when parse fails. 2) re-ask flow: if parse fails, call model again with "You returned malformed JSON (trailing comma/missing bracket). Please produce only valid JSON matching schema X." 3) exponential backoff + jitter on retries.

maya_support: here's a compact repair snippet we recommend customers try client-side before escalating: 
```js
// pseudo
function tryParseJoined(s){
  try { return JSON.parse(s); }
  catch(e){
    // strip trailing commas in arrays/objects
    s = s.replace(/,\s*([}\]])/g, '$1');
    // attempt to close unbalanced brackets
    const open = (s.match(/[\[\{]/g)||[]).length;
    const close = (s.match(/[\}\]]/g)||[]).length;
    if(close < open) s += ']'.repeat(open - close);
    return JSON.parse(s);
  }
}
```

maya_support: also add a re-ask prompt tone: `You must respond with strictly valid JSON adhering to ...` — keep it short to reduce hallucinated commentary.

jon_customer: will try that. question: is this safe for structured output where content can be multi-line with code blocks?

alex_ml: yes, but be careful: postprocess regex is last-resort — prefer schema nudges and explicit "json_only" instructions in the system prompt, and set streaming to false for critical writes if latency allows. For streaming keep a small buffer/join timeout before parse.

kevin_sre: infra action: I'm going to increase stream keepalive and add a short grace window in the proxy so we don't cut off trailing bytes during preemption. If we push a config, will ping here.

ops-bot: deploy started: stream-proxy/grace-window v2 -> staging (canary 10%).

maya_support: operational checklist for support when customer reports JSON parse errors: 1) collect raw joined response 2) check for trailing commas/truncation 3) try local postprocess regex 4) attempt re-ask with strict schema prompt 5) if still failing, capture server-side trace id + model shard + serving node and escalate to eng-sre.

jon_customer: trying quick fix now, will report results. Appreciate the repair snippet.

maya_support: if you want a temporary suggestion to reduce risk: set stream=false for these critical calls while we stabilize proxy; also add retry with backoff: 3 attempts, base 200ms, factor 2, jitter +-50ms.

kevin_sre: noted. I'll also keep an eye on the canary logs. If we see repro at canary we will rollback.

maya_support: tagging this as escalation pending: assign to alex_ml for model prompt tweaks and kevin_sre for infra. Update #7891 with steps and outcomes. :thumbsup:

jon_customer: confirmed client-side regex + re-ask removed the parse error in initial tests. will run load test and report. thanks!
